<title>THAILAND: Thai finmin says no plan to intervene in baht.</title>
<headline>Thai finmin says no plan to intervene in baht.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Monday the government has no plan to intervene in the forex market to stabilise the baht, which is falling against the surging U.S. dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;The easing of the baht reflects the the dollar's trend against other majors and not speculative attacks because our economy has stabilised,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
</text>
